Execute Phase 2 only.

Implement Supabase authentication and application persistence.

FEATURES
- Sign-in/sign-out.
- Session handling.
- Project create/read/update/delete.
- Project types: story, product-ad, repurpose.
- Stable IDs.
- Versioned schemas.
- Safe migrations.
- Save/conflict states.

DATABASE
Create suitable tables for:
- Profiles/workspaces.
- Projects and revisions.
- Scenes.
- Media metadata.
- Sources and claims.
- Generation proposals.
- Provider jobs.
- Usage ledger.
- Render snapshots/results.

Use JSON columns only where appropriate.
Do not turn all entities into an unvalidated document blob.

SECURITY
Enable and test row-level security.
Users must not read or modify another user's projects.
Server privileged access must perform explicit ownership checks.
Never accept owner_id supplied by the client as authorization.

Do not create a public shared project database.

TEST
Two-user isolation, expired sessions, unauthorized requests,
project reload, migration, conflicts, and deletion.

ACCEPTANCE
Authorized users can persist their own projects;
other users cannot access them.

Stop after Phase 2.
